A||||9||Lizzy||Check Engine Light?||||11||
Z||000000||Lizzy||06-05-2001||06:21 PM||||I could use some advice, When I start my 4cylinder it idles at 2500-3000 for about a minute then the check engine light comes on and it seems to idle better.  The light stays on the entire time.  Where should I start checking to fix this?||||reg||11
Z||000001||theogre||06-05-2001||06:26 PM||||Something is causing a problem that is setting DTC's (error codes) in the engine computer.<P>You need to read the codes or have them read before you do anything.<P>Best thing for you to do at this point, if you are going to try to fix this yourself is go to a parts store and get a Fiero book by Haynes or Chiltons. You may have to order it at some stores.<P>The book has all the codes and how to read them. Should give you a starting point...||||reg||1
Z||000002||sqoach||06-05-2001||06:30 PM||||Check the computer to see what code it is. Then go from there. To check the computer, you take off the cigarette lighter trim plate (15 torx bit) and you'll see the computer terminal thingy. Get a piece of wire or a paperclip and ground the A and B terminals. <P>This will make your check engine light blink. First it will give a code 12, then any codes after that.<P><BR>Edited because I don't know what I'm doing  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>[This message has been edited by sqoach (edited 06-05-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by sqoach (edited 06-05-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||06-05-2001||07:28 PM||||it blinks for the first digit, then quick space, then blinks for second digit-then long gap.<P>code 12  =  blink-short space-blink blink-long space then repeats||||reg||1
Z||000004||Steve Normington||06-05-2001||07:53 PM||||Everytime I get a Check Engine light, I'll short out the terminals and get 12 and nothing else. When I then take it to the dealer, they can get the codes every time. Should the engine be running or not when checking the codes. The last codes they got were for a bad O2 and EGR valve, I never got anything but 12.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Indiana_resto_guy||06-05-2001||09:18 PM||||Steve,<BR>Engine off, key on.<P>Liz,<BR>I can't remember the #, but it willindicate a high idle. This sets after engine holds that RPM for over 30 seconds. Causes if I remember correctly are MAP sensor and IAC valve. (I think)||||reg||1
Z||000006||Lizzy||06-06-2001||08:29 AM||||Where is the MAP and The IAC sensors? I have a chiltons book but they are not in there.||||reg||1
Z||000007||87GTZ34||06-06-2001||08:52 AM||||Lizzy,  I'm not sure if you got procedure for checking codes but here goes:<BR>1) make sure car is off<BR>2) remove access at cig lighter<BR>3) connect A to B which is the lower two<BR>   positions on the passenger side<BR>4) turn key to ON position but don't start it<BR>5) watch check eng light blink 1-2, 1-2, 1-2 is normal operation and anyting else should be codes.  It repeats 3 times and moves on to the next code if any.<BR>To reset codes, disconnect the ground term for &gt; 10 secs.<P>IAC on Duke is mounted on the TBI unit. It has 4 wires and the TPS is on the opposite side and it has 3 wires.  You want 4 wires.<P>MAP is on the intake toward the passenger side.<P> GL||||reg||1
Z||000008||Indiana_resto_guy||06-06-2001||08:53 AM||||MAP, on breather. IAC, on throttle body.<BR>Do you know how to pull codes and please state year.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Lizzy||06-06-2001||11:33 AM||||Thanks everyone. I decided to take the car to the garage, who sponsors my race car, and he got the codes for me.  A lot of codes came up but it was just the coolant temp sensor fouling everything up, which he gave me. I put it in and everything cleared up. Again thanks for the helpful advice.||||reg||14
